\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Father Divine, I come to Thee,
\par I yield, a captive, to Thy sway,
\par That love's gold chain may set me free
\par For all the burden of the day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I come not to avoid my care,
\par I come not to desert the strife;
\par I come to seek new strength to bear,
\par I fly to find new power for life.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Many there be that seek Thy face
\par To meet the hour of parting breath,
\par But 'tis for earth I need Thy grace-
\par Life is more solemn still than death.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. When morning glids the porch of day,
\par I feel so vile amid the glow
\par That I should faint, didst Thou not say:
\par I make thee whiter than the snow.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. When noontide brings its work to all,
\par I find my task so hard to be,
\par That I should sink, didst Thou not call:
\par My strength is perfected in Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. When darkness leads the world to rest,
\par The silent burden of the night
\par Would crush, but for Thy message blest:
\par At evening time there shall be light.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O may these streams of golden light,
\par To all my desert way be given,
\par Till faith itself is lost in sight,
\par And days on earth be days of heaven.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

